<title>GERMANY: Warm, rainy weather aids crops in Germany.</title>
<headline>Warm, rainy weather aids crops in Germany.</headline>
<dateline>OFFENBACH 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Frequent showers and warm weather favour Germany's grain, oilseeds and sugar beet crops, the DWD national meteorological institute said.</p>
<p>&quot;Soil moisture levels are very good apart from some eastern German regions which are not crucial to the overall harvest,&quot; a DWD source said.</p>
<p>DWD had recorded an even and slow ripening of rapeseed and cereals and saw good yield prospects for winter wheat.</p>
<p>Temperatures in the coming week were forecast at 18-22 degrees, which would help all crops except maize.</p>
<p>Farmers organisations said rains had interrupted work schedules in areas such as the harvesting of potatoes.</p>
<p>They were also worried by lodging as a result of the rains.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom, +49-40-41903275</p>
